            <div xml:id="d395-a1">

                <pb facs="0516" n="432" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg432"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum.</hi></head>
                <p>The Imperial Government has accepted the proposition of submitting its claims
                    against the Venezuelan Government to arbitration under certain conditions, which
                    are communicated at the same time herewith to the American ambassador, and has
                    therein expressed the wish that the President of the United States should accept
                    the duties of arbitrator.</p>
                <p>In common with the British Government, the Imperial Government believes that it
                    has found in this way every guaranty for a satisfactory solution of the
                    difficulty, so that this course deserves to have precedence accorded to it over
                    the course recently proposed by the Venezuelan Government, namely, that the two
                    powers should negotiate through the American minister, Mr. Bowen, as
                    intermediary.</p>
            </div>
